  <text id="shot-label" x="70" y="144" width="712" height="14" font="caption" size="11" color="muted" align="center" wrap="false">Real web screenshot • browser-rendered parcel map with multiple markers, active legends, and corridor overlays</text>
  <shape id="right-card" type="rect" x="826" y="136" width="396" height="428" fill="mist" stroke="hairline" stroke-width="1"/>
  <text id="right-title" x="850" y="162" width="348" height="28" font="body" size="20" color="ink"><p><strong>What this unlocks for Lagos</strong></p></text>
  <text id="right-copy" x="850" y="204" width="348" height="316" font="body" size="17" color="ink" line-height="1.33">
    <p>The map view lets officers and executive reviewers see parcel location, overlay context, and selected parcel intelligence in one web workspace.</p>
    <p space-before="14"><strong>For Lagos, this supports:</strong></p>
    <p space-before="10">• Housing growth review and parcel prioritisation.</p>
    <p>• Right-of-way and corridor conflict screening before field escalation.</p>
    <p>• Faster desk-based review of parcel status, workflow stage, and risk.</p>
    <p>• More credible coordination between land administration, planning, infrastructure, and builder-facing approvals.</p>
    <p space-before="14">Because this is a real web map screenshot from the live product, the deck can now show genuine geospatial evidence rather than only describing parcel intelligence in theory.</p>
  </text>
  <shape id="assurance-band" type="rect" x="58" y="586" width="1164" height="40" fill="#ECFDF5" stroke="#BBF7D0" stroke-width="1"/>
  <text id="assurance" x="82" y="598" width="1116" height="16" font="body" size="15" color="ink" align="center" wrap="false">The Lagos procurement case is strengthened when map context, parcel identity, and legal workflow are visible in one review surface.</text>
